     TFs with R^2 > 0.8:    21% of real-regulon TFs

B. GEOMETRY LEVEL (real regulons):
     Spearman rho(D_expression, D_TF)        median 0.342  (ALL 29 views, B1)
     Spearman rho(W_fused, W_expression)     median 0.770
     ARI(fused partition, expression-only)   k=2  median 0.793
     ARI(fused partition, expression-only)   k=3  median 0.652

HOW TO READ THIS
----------------
High Part-A R^2 means the TF view is largely a linear re-encoding of
expression features the model already has. High Part-B ARI means the
fused partition is close to the one expression alone would have
produced. Together they convert the null of scripts 07 and 14 from an
observation into an explanation: there was little independent
information available to add, so no method operating on this feature
space could have added much.

If instead Part-A R^2 is LOW and Part-B ARI is HIGH, the conclusion
changes: independent information existed and SNF discarded it, which
is a criticism of the fusion method rather than of the TF view. Both
outcomes are reportable; they are reported differently.

